{
  "name": "hellas-consensus",
  "description": "Hellas-consensus implements high-throughput BFT primitives designed for partially synchronous environments, specifically targeting the Autobahn and Morpheus protocol families. It employs a DAG-based data dissemination layer coupled with a quorum-driven consensus mechanism to achieve optimistic responsivity and robust recovery from network blips. The project maintains a multi-language formal verification suite using Coq, Isabelle, Lean, and TLA+ to ensure the correctness of its bisimulation relations and protocol state transitions.",
